{title: 191 - Love Divine}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #191 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 191}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Love divine, [Fm]all [Eb]loves [Fm/C]excelling, [Eb/Bb]Joy of [Ab]heaven, [Gdim]to [Fm]earth [Ab]come [Fm]down;
[Eb]Fix in [Eb7/Db]us Thy [Cm]humble [Eb]dwelling, [Fm]All [Eb]Thy [Fm/C]faithful [Eb/Bb]mercies [Ab]crown!
[Fm]Jesus, [Db]Thou [Cm]art [Ab]all [Eb/G]compassion, Pure, [Ab]unbounded love Thou [Gdim]art;
[Fm]Visit us with [Em]Thy [Cm]salvation, [Db]Enter [Cm]every [Bbm]trembling [Eb7/Db]heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Breathe, O breathe [Fm/C]thy [Eb/Bb]loving [Gdim]Spirit
[Eb]into every [Gdim]troubled [Ab]breast!
[Eb]Let [Eb7/Db]us [Cm]all [Eb]in [Fm]thee inherit;
[Eb]let [Eb7/Db]us [Cm]find [Eb]the promised rest.
[Fm]Take [Db]away [Eb/G]our bent [Ab]to sinning;
[Fm]Alpha [Ab]and [Eb]Omega [Ab]be;
[Fm]end of [Em]faith, [Cm]as [Db]its [Cm]beginning,
[Fm]set our [Cm]hearts at liberty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Come, Almighty to [Ab]deliver,
[Eb]let us all thy grace [Gdim]receive;
[Eb]suddenly return [Fm/C]and [Eb/Bb]never,
[Eb]nevermore thy temples leave.
[Fm]Thee [Db]we [Ab]would [Eb/G]be always [Ab]blessing,
[Fm]serve [Db]thee [Ab]as [Eb]thy hosts [Db/Ab]above,
[Fm]pray and [Em]praise [Cm]thee [Db]without [Bbm]ceasing,
[Fm]glory [Cm]in thy perfect [Eb/Bb]love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]Finish, then, thy new [Gdim]creation;
[Eb]pure and spotless let [Gdim]us [Ab]be.
[Eb]Let [Eb7/Db]us [Cm]see [Eb]thy [Fm]great salvation
[Eb]perfectly restored in thee;
[Fm]changed [Db]from [Ab]glory [Eb]into [Ab]glory,
[Fm]till [Db]in [Ab]heaven [Eb]we [Ab]take our place,
[Fm]till we [Em]cast [Cm]our [Db]crowns [Cm]before [Eb/Bb]thee,
[Fm]lost in [Cm]wonder, love, [Bbm]and [Eb/Bb]praise.
{end_of_verse}
